/loop You are executing the Palmly UI/UX redesign ("Quiet Cosmos"). Work autonomously and continue until every redesign task is done or you are blocked.

GROUNDING (do this at the start of every iteration, before any work):
1. Read Planning/UIUX-Redesign.md IN FULL — it is the design source of truth (palette/token spec, typography, elevation/shape/motion, the KEEP/SOFTEN/REMOVE heritage decisions, tone, the two server-rendered surfaces, and the verification approach). Founder-locked direction: calm & premium (Headspace/Calm feel), heritage as subtle hints only (keep the softened cinnabar accent + the traced-palm hero; drop CJK glyphs 心智命运 + seal chrome; English-first), sans-first typography, full journey in scope.
2. Read Planning/UIUX-Redesign-Tasks.md IN FULL — the checkbox task ledger (STATE block + Execution Protocol + tasks R1..R24). This is the machine you execute.
3. For the screen/flow you are about to touch, read its behavior/content spec in Planning/UIUX-specs.md, and READ the current source file(s) before editing (match surrounding style).

EXECUTE:
4. Follow the ledger's EXECUTION PROTOCOL literally: pick the first task in document order whose checkbox is [ ] or [~]; build it to the north star using ONLY design tokens (no raw hexes in components) and realistic, non-lorem content; run its Verify line; and ONLY when verification actually passes, mark it [x] with today's date, append a Build Log line with evidence, update the STATE block, and git commit as "R#.T# <description>". Then proceed to the next task.
5. Verify device-free, like the existing checkpoints: static gates first (from app/: `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`; for edge-function tasks also the Deno tests), then a visual check via `npx expo export --platform web` + a headless-Chrome screenshot at 390x844 (and 320 wide where clipping matters), saved under docs/checkpoints/redesign/. The /dev route map walks every route; /dev/theme is the design-system regression surface. For native-only surfaces (camera capture, RevenueCat paywall) and reanimated motion that won't render in web export: build with fixture/mock stand-ins so the LAYOUT is screenshot-verifiable, verify the static end-state, and mark the on-device leg [~]. NEVER report a green you did not actually see.
6. NEVER mark a task [x] without its Verify passing. NEVER skip or reorder tasks (R1..R10 foundation must land before the screen tasks). If a task fails 3 genuinely different approaches, mark it [!], record what you tried under it, set STATE "Blocked on", and move to the next unblocked task.
7. Standing rules: do NOT break backend/edge-function logic, auth, realtime, or the device-gated stubs — this is a visual/UX overhaul, not new features (the only server edits are re-skinning the SVG/HTML in R16b/R16c). Preserve ThemeProvider's forceScheme prop (the /dev/theme harness needs it). Ship back-compat token aliases in R1 rather than rename-and-break. Every new svg icon gets an accessibilityLabel; every new animation gets a reduce-motion fallback. Migrations/secrets: unchanged — none of this touches the DB schema. Decisions the docs don't cover: pick the simplest option that matches the north star and note it in the ledger.

LOOP CONTROL:
8. Keep completing tasks while context allows. Before context runs low, finish or cleanly park the in-flight task as [~] with a resume note, update STATE, commit everything, and end the iteration — the next iteration re-grounds from step 1.
9. If ALL remaining work is blocked ([!] or genuinely needs me), give me a clear list of exactly what you need, then STOP the loop.
10. When every task is [x] (or the rest are [!]), report it and stop the loop.
11. End every iteration with a short status report: tasks completed this run (with screenshot/test evidence), current STATE, and anything you need from me.
